## Run it

```bash
tvbo validate study .                 # the tree and the filenames conform to the layout
tvbo run {study}.yaml                 # the nested studies depth first, then manuscript_results.yml
tvbo run {study}.yaml --manifest-only # re-emit the manifest from containers that already exist
tvbo verify {study}.yaml              # every quoted number resolves and no analysis is stale
cd docs && quarto render              # manuscript.pdf
```

`manuscript_results.yml` is committed: the document reads it through Quarto `metadata-files`, so it renders in a checkout that has none of the run containers. Each nested study runs and is reported on its own terms — its results stay in its own `derivatives/`, and its claims in its own `docs/analysis/`.
